WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
A toy car moves. A dry bean sits still.

2
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.260
Which one is alive?

3
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:11.980
Use this twenty-five-minute sort to help your child practice looking closely.

4
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.800
They make a rule and check it against what they find.

5
00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.730
Fill a basket with ten to twelve household things.

6
00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:26.450
Start with a houseplant, an apple, a dry leaf, a stick, and a shell.

7
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.730
Add a rock, a spoon, and a toy car.

8
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:32.430
Set out paper and a pencil.

9
00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:35.990
Use one or two large dry kitchen beans.

10
00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:38.930
Skip garden-shop seed packets.

11
00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:45.193
First, ask your child to sort everything into two piles, alive and not alive.

12
00:00:46.553 --> 00:00:48.133
Hold back from correcting them.

13
00:00:49.373 --> 00:00:53.813
Instead, ask, how did you decide, and write down their rule in their own words.

14
00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:57.913
Listening first lets your child test their own idea.

15
00:00:58.967 --> 00:01:02.127
Compare the rock with a plant, a pet, or your child.

16
00:01:03.487 --> 00:01:05.447
Ask, what does it do that the rock does not?

17
00:01:06.707 --> 00:01:11.827
Write four clues together: grows, needs water, air and food, reacts, and makes more

18
00:01:11.827 --> 00:01:15.187
of its kind. Plants use light to make food.

19
00:01:16.387 --> 00:01:17.787
Check all four clues together.

20
00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:21.370
Try the checklist on the rock together first.

21
00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:26.770
Then let your child test each object and move it if their answer changes.

22
00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:31.110
With the car, ask, does it grow or make a baby car?

23
00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:33.690
A dry seed is still alive.

24
00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:36.510
Water and warmth let it sprout.

25
00:01:37.483 --> 00:01:40.243
Now picture the dry leaf sitting on your table.

26
00:01:41.463 --> 00:01:46.283
If you are using just two piles, living and nonliving, pause and decide for

27
00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:50.563
yourself. Which pile does that dry leaf belong in, and why?

28
00:01:56.117 --> 00:01:59.117
For this sort, use Virginia’s kindergarten rule.

29
00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:04.517
The dry leaf goes in the living pile because it was part of a living plant.

30
00:02:05.877 --> 00:02:07.157
A rock goes in nonliving.

31
00:02:08.437 --> 00:02:13.177
For ages eight to ten, split the living pile into alive now and once alive.

32
00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.840
Stay with your child throughout the activity.

33
00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:22.800
Keep all small objects, including large beans, away from children under four.

34
00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.240
Keep everything in the basket out of mouths.

35
00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.740
Count the beans back into a lidded jar yourself.

36
00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.620
If a child is choking or struggling to breathe, call nine one one.

37
00:02:35.933 --> 00:02:40.633
On your optional ten-minute walk, find three living and three nonliving things.

38
00:02:41.973 --> 00:02:44.693
Stay on a permitted path away from roads and water.

39
00:02:46.013 --> 00:02:48.353
Stay within arm’s reach near roads or water.

40
00:02:49.693 --> 00:02:52.713
Never leave your child alone near water of any depth.

41
00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:55.033
Look without picking.

42
00:02:56.353 --> 00:02:59.633
Wash hands with soap and water and check for ticks afterward.

43
00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:05.767
In this game, your child practices looking closely and stating a rule out loud.

44
00:03:06.987 --> 00:03:11.827
They test that rule against tricky objects and revise it when evidence pushes back.

45
00:03:13.107 --> 00:03:17.287
One clue alone can fool you, so checking every sign together is what counts.
